    "title": "Executable masquerading by file extension",
    "desc": "A script was executed under a document or media file name - a shell run over a file ending in .png/.pdf/.jpg/.doc... (an executable hiding as an image), or a binary whose name carries a double extension like report.pdf.sh. Giving a payload a harmless-looking extension is how an attacker gets a user (or a careless automation) to run it and how it blends into a listing (MITRE T1036.007 / T1036.008). A normal `sh script.sh` or `python app.py` is not matched; a shell running image.png, or a .pdf.sh being executed, is.",
